      "statement": "Desktop exit and shell callbacks are guarded by the connection controller's attempt ID, while mobile consumes SSH events in a generation-guarded stream. Desktop recovery scheduling belongs to RemoteSessionConnectionController, which invokes model-supplied teardown before presenting recovery or arming retry; SSHSessionModel resets shell state and retires channel work, then starts a fresh attempt and recaptures integration settings on retry, retaining responsibility for startup configuration and cwd consumption. PTY close clears shell/runtime state and may retain transport for sibling SFTP or explicit control ownership. Runtime exec uses the existing authenticated transport with immediate capacity admission, no channel-open retry, a two-second timeout and 1 MiB output bound; refusal conservatively withholds control capabilities without disabling terminal I/O.",
